# Build trees, which hold everything generated: the C++ layer, the
# specification's tables and the test fixtures (R-7). The two globs rather
# than literals: -asan, -xcode and whatever the next configuration is called
# all belong here.  Deliberately NOT /build*:
# git folds case on case-insensitive filesystems (macOS APFS), so that pattern
# also swallows the root BUILD.bazel and the file never gets committed.
/build/
/build-*/

# Bazel convenience symlinks (see .bazelrc --symlink_prefix). MODULE.bazel.lock
# is committed on purpose: it pins the resolved module graph.
/bazel-*

# macOS Finder droppings, at any depth.
.DS_Store

# Slide files, anywhere.  The corpus is hosted and fetched (see
# plans/phase-6-corpus.md); fixtures produced or downloaded locally are never
# committed, which is the whole point of pinning them by digest instead.
*.iris
*.test_slide

# Fetched dependencies (Iris-Headers).  Pulled by CMake into a fixed path so
# tooling can find them; never part of this repository.
/.deps
.vscode
__pycache__/
.arbiter/

# Handoff documents, at any depth. These are working notes between sessions —
# a record of what was measured and what fooled us, superseded the moment the
# next session measures again. They are never part of the repository: what
# survives a handoff belongs in development/, CLAUDE.md, or a test that
# asserts it. Ignored rather than merely uncommitted so `git add -A` cannot
# quietly promote one to a permanent document.
*handoff*.md
